<BaseLayout title="Squadfire — Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy of Squadfire, an app by Little Monge Studios" lang="en">
  <h1>Squadfire — Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 2026-10-03</p>

  <p>
    This policy describes what data Squadfire ("the app") collects, why,
    who it's shared with, and how you can access or delete it. It's
    written to match exactly what the app's code does — not a generic
    template.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p>
    Squadfire is developed by an individual developer (a private person,
    not an incorporated company) operating as "Little Monge Studios",
    based in Spain. Contact:
    <a href="mailto:team@littlemongestudios.com">team@littlemongestudios.com</a>.
    This person is the data controller under the EU General Data
    Protection Regulation (GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>No account required, sign-in with Google is optional</h2>
  <p>
    When you first open the app, it creates an <strong>anonymous
    account</strong> — a random identifier with no personal information
    attached — so your streak and settings can be saved. You choose a
    username right away (never your real name, and never taken from
    anywhere else).
  </p>
  <p>
    ⚠️ Because an anonymous account is tied to this install, <strong>if
    you uninstall the app or clear its data without signing in first,
    your streak cannot be recovered.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    You can optionally link a Google account from Settings so your
    progress survives a reinstall or a new phone. Linking keeps the same
    account (same streak, cosmetics, friends and squads). If you link
    Google, we store your Google account's email address, only to show
    it back to you in Settings as confirmation you're linked; we never
    use it for anything else and never show it to other users.
  </p>
  <p>
    On a new phone or after reinstalling, you can get back to that
    account with <strong>Continue with Google</strong>. If you had
    already started playing anonymously on that phone, the app asks
    before switching, and that anonymous account and its data are then
    deleted — progress can't be merged between two accounts.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <p>Tied to your account id, in our database (hosted on Supabase, EU region — Ireland):</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Profile:</strong> the username you chose (or the auto-generated "Player a1b2c3d4"), your avatar (one of the app's pre-designed illustrations — you can't upload a photo), and the profile frame, name style and title you equipped.</li>
    <li><strong>Google email</strong>, only if you linked Google (see above).</li>
    <li><strong>Check-ins and streaks:</strong> the dates you checked in, your current and best streak, your streak-freeze balance and when you used one. The monthly puzzle, stickers and achievements are worked out from these dates — nothing extra is tracked for them.</li>
    <li><strong>Time zone:</strong> your phone's time zone name (for example "Europe/Madrid"), so a check-in counts for your calendar day, plus a short history of when it changed (to limit abuse when travelling). We don't use it to locate you.</li>
    <li><strong>Points and the Shop:</strong> your points balance and how you earned or spent them (check-ins, achievements, completed months, goals, squad milestones, streak wagers), and the cosmetic items you bought with points. Points are an in-app currency with no money value.</li>
    <li><strong>Streak goal:</strong> the goal you picked (7, 14 or 30 days), when, and when you reached it.</li>
    <li><strong>Streak wager:</strong> when you bet points on keeping your streak for a week, the dates it covers and whether you won. It depends only on your own check-ins — there's no chance involved and no real money.</li>
    <li><strong>Monthly bonus wheel:</strong> for each month you completed, the multiplier you got and the bonus points.</li>
    <li><strong>Friends and invites:</strong> who you're connected with, any invite code you generate (it expires), and, if someone joined with your code, that link (to credit the invite reward).</li>
    <li><strong>Squads:</strong> the squads you created or joined, who invited whom, when each member joined or left, and the squad's milestones. Squad streaks are worked out from members' check-in dates.</li>
    <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> a device push token for each phone where you've allowed notifications, with the platform and the app language, and whether you want squad notifications. Deleted when you delete your account, and automatically when the push service reports the token is no longer valid.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety:</strong> the people you've blocked and the reports you've sent (who, the reason, the optional text, and when). Reports about you are also stored, with the reporter's account id, so we can review them.</li>
    <li><strong>Terms of Use:</strong> which version you accepted, and when.</li>
    <li><strong>Achievements</strong> you've unlocked, and when.</li>
    <li><strong>Purchases:</strong> if you buy a streak-freeze pack, the store's transaction id, the product and the date (see "Purchases").</li>
    <li><strong>App usage events</strong> (see "App usage analytics").</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not collect your real name, phone number, precise or
    approximate location, contacts, photos, or any government ID. Saving
    a completed monthly illustration to your gallery only needs
    permission to add an image — the app never reads your photos.
  </p>

  <h2>What other players can see</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone using Squadfire can see, next to your username in the
    rankings and on your public profile: your avatar, profile frame,
    name style and title, your current and best streak, your number of
    check-ins in the current month (season ranking), and which stickers
    you've unlocked. Members of a squad you're in also see whether
    you've checked in today, and can poke you. Nothing else — not your
    Google email, your friends list, your points, your purchases, your
    time zone or your check-in dates.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you share an image (your streak, the monthly puzzle, an
    illustration or your stickers), it includes your invite code, a QR
    code and a link to download the app. You choose where to share it;
    we don't see it.
  </p>

  <h2>Blocking and reporting</h2>
  <p>
    You can block any player from their profile: you stop seeing each
    other in friends and rankings, they can't poke you, any friendship
    between you is removed, and you can no longer be in a squad together
    (if you share one, one of you leaves it). You can unblock them from
    Settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also report a player (offensive username, harassment, spam
    or other). Reports are only visible to us, reviewed manually, and
    used solely to keep the app safe — for example, resetting an
    offensive username. We don't tell the reported player who reported
    them. Usernames are also checked automatically against a list of
    offensive words.
  </p>

  <h2>App usage analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We record a small set of in-app events, tied to your account id, in
    the same database as everything above — never sent to a third-party
    analytics service: app opens, check-ins, streaks lost, streak
    freezes used, cosmetics unlocked, the post-check-in celebration
    being shown or skipped, shares and illustration downloads / "set as
    wallpaper" (and whether they failed, with the error message and your
    Android version), invites used, linking or recovering a Google
    account, pokes sent (and why one couldn't be delivered), public
    profiles viewed, avatar changes, blocks, reports, accepting the
    Terms of Use, achievements, choosing and reaching a streak goal,
    creating a squad and its milestones, streak wagers placed, won or
    lost, and the in-app rating prompt being shown. This tells us which
    parts of the app are used and what breaks — no session recording, no
    location, no advertising profile.
  </p>

  <h2>Crash reports (Sentry)</h2>
  <p>
    When crash reporting is enabled, if the app crashes or hits an error
    it sends a technical report to Sentry (Functional Software, Inc.):
    the error and where in the code it happened, the app version, your
    device model and operating-system version, and the environment. It
    doesn't include your username, email, check-ins or any content you
    created.
  </p>

  <h2>Notifications</h2>
  <p>
    All notifications are optional and need your phone's permission. The
    app asks for it only after your first check-in or first friend,
    explaining why first, and Settings has a switch for each kind:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Daily reminder, last chance (at 21:00 if you haven't checked in and your streak is at risk) and come back (the day after you lose a streak, and once more after 3 days without opening the app — then nothing else). These are scheduled on your phone: no data about them is sent to us or anyone else.</li>
    <li>
      Pokes from friends or squad members, new friend notices, squad
      invitations and "everyone in your squad but you has checked in".
      These are real push notifications sent from our server through
      Expo's push service and delivered by Firebase Cloud Messaging
      (Google) on Android or Apple Push Notification service on iOS.
      Those services receive the device token and the notification text,
      per
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>
      and
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Advertising (AdMob)</h2>
  <p>
    Watching a short video ad lets you earn a streak freeze. Ads are
    served by Google AdMob, which — separately from us — may collect
    device and advertising identifiers (such as the Android advertising
    ID) to serve and measure ads, per
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.
    You can reset or delete your advertising ID in your phone's
    settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Ratings</h2>
  <p>
    After a good moment (a 7-day streak or a perfect month) the app may
    ask Google Play to show its rating dialog — at most once every few
    months, and never right after you lose a streak. Google decides
    whether it appears; your rating goes to Google Play, not to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Purchases (in-app purchases)</h2>
  <p>
    If you buy a streak-freeze pack, the purchase is handled entirely by
    Google Play (or the App Store) — <strong>we never see or store your
    payment card details.</strong> We only store the store's transaction
    id (to credit your freezes and prevent being charged twice), the
    product and the date.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell your data and don't share it for advertising. We use
    these service providers, only for the purposes above:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> (database, sign-in and server functions; EU region).</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> — Sign-In (only if you link Google), Firebase Cloud Messaging (push delivery), AdMob (rewarded ads) and Google Play (purchases, ratings).</li>
    <li><strong>Expo</strong> (push notification relay).</li>
    <li><strong>Sentry</strong> (crash reports, when enabled).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Legal basis and your rights (GDPR)</h2>
  <p>
    We process your data to provide the app you asked for (performance
    of a contract), to keep it safe and working (legitimate interest:
    abuse limits, reports, crash reports, usage analytics), and, for
    notifications and ads, based on the permissions you give on your
    phone.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can ask us for a copy of your data, to correct it, to delete it,
    to restrict or object to its processing, or to receive it in a
    portable format, by writing to
    <a href="mailto:team@littlemongestudios.com">team@littlemongestudios.com</a>.
    If you think we haven't handled your data properly, you can complain
    to the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD,
    <a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aepd.es</a>)
    or your local authority.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is kept while your account exists. When you delete your
    account, everything tied to it is deleted immediately and
    permanently (our database removes every related record
    automatically). Removed records may survive in our hosting
    provider's encrypted backups for a limited time before those backups
    expire.
  </p>

  <h2>Data deletion</h2>
  <p>
    You can permanently delete your account and everything tied to it at
    any time from <strong>Profile → Settings → Delete my account</strong>
    — it's immediate and can't be undone. If you've lost access to the
    app, see
    <a href="/squadfire/delete-account/">https://littlemongestudios.com/squadfire/delete-account</a>
    to request deletion by email.
  </p>

  <h2>Terms of Use</h2>
  <p>
    Using Squadfire's social features (username, friends, squads,
    rankings, public profile) requires accepting the
    <a href="/squadfire/terms/">Terms of Use</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Squadfire is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age
    for digital consent in your country — 14 in Spain) and we don't
    knowingly collect their data. If you believe a child has created an
    account, write to us and we'll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the "Last updated" date at the top changes
    too, and for important changes the app will tell you. Continued use
    of the app after a change means you accept the updated policy.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
